--- !u!114 &5288353682515988936
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3935354042040367315}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "CRIEFF PTE. LTD. (hereinafter referred to as \"Company\") establishes
    and discloses the following personal information processing policies to protect
    the personal information of information subjects and to handle users' complaints
    quickly and smoothly under Article 30 of the Personal Information Protection
    Act.\n\nThis Privacy Policy applies to defenGO (hereinafter referred to as \"Services\")
    provided by \"Company\".\n\n**Article 1 (Purpose of Processing Personal Information)**\n\n\"Company\"
    processes personal information for the following purposes: The personal information
    being processed will not be used for any of the following purposes, and if the
    purpose of use is changed, necessary measures will be implemented, such as obtaining
    separate consent under Article 18 of the Personal Information Protection Act.\n\n1.
    Personal information items collected when signing up for membership or using
    services\n- Member registration: e-mail address, social login account information\n-
    Self-certification: Name, mobile phone number, date of birth, gender, domestic/foreign
    information, registered carrier, identity verification information (DI) (Separate
    consent process by identity verification agency will be carried out.)\n1. Use
    in marketing and advertising\n- Personal information is processed for the purpose
    of providing event and advertising information and opportunities to participate.\n\n**Article
    2 (Processing and Retaining Period of Personal Information)**\n\n1. \"company\"
    processes and holds personal information within the period of holding and using
    personal information or the period of holding and using personal information
    agreed upon when collecting personal information from the data subject under
    the Act.\n2. Each personal information processing and holding period is as follows.\n3.
    Sign up and manage \"service\" membership\n- Collection of personal information
    related to \"service\" membership registration and management. Held for the above
    purpose of use up to three years from the date of consent for use. It\u2019s
    being used.\n- Grounds for possession: User information for processing requests,
    such as access to personal information\n- Related Acts and subordinate statutes:
    Records on the collection/processing, use, etc. of credit information: 3 years\n-
    Reason for exception\n\n**Article 3 (Items of personal information to be processed)**\n\n1.
    \"Company\" is processing the following personal information items\n2. Sign up
    and manage \"service\" membership\n- Required: Email, social login account information\n\n**Article
    4 (Procedure and Method of Destruction of Personal Information)**\n\n1. The \"company\"
    shall destroy the personal information without delay when personal information
    becomes unnecessary, such as the lapse of the personal information retention
    period and the achievement of the purpose of processing. \n2. If the personal
    information retention period agreed by the data subject has elapsed or the purpose
    of processing has been achieved, the personal information shall be transferred
    to a separate database (DB) or stored in a different storage place. \n3. The
    procedures and methods of destroying personal information are as follows.\n   
    1. Destruction procedure\n\nThe \"company\" selects personal information on which
    the reason for destruction occurred, and destroys personal information with the
    approval of the personal information protection manager of the \"company\". \n\n1.
    Destruction method \n- The information in the form of an electronic file uses
    a technical method that does not allow the recording to be played back.\n- Personal
    information printed on paper is shredded or destroyed by incineration\n\n**Article
    5 (Matters concerning the rights and obligations of the information subject and
    legal representative, and the method of exercising them)**\n\n1. The information
    subject may exercise the right to view, correct, delete, and request suspension
    of processing of personal information to the \"company\" at any time. \n2. The
    exercise of rights under paragraph (1) may be made in writing, e-mail, facsimile
    (FAX) in accordance with Article 41 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal
    Information Protection Act, and the \"Company\" will take action without delay.
    \n3. The exercise of rights under paragraph (1) may be conducted through an agent,
    such as a legal representative of the information subject or a person entrusted.
    In such cases, \"Public Notice on the Method of Processing Personal Information
    (No. 2020-7)\" You must submit a power of attorney in attached Form 11. \n4.
    Requests for access to personal information and suspension of processing may
    be restricted under Articles 35 (4) and 37 (2) of the Personal Information Protection
    Act. \n5. A request for correction and deletion of personal information cannot
    be requested if the personal information is specified as the subject of collection
    in other laws and regulations. \n6. The \"company\" verifies whether the person
    who made the request for perusal, correction or deletion, or suspension of processing,
    etc. according to the right of the information subject is himself/herself or
    a legitimate agent.\n\n**Article 6 (Matters concerning measures to secure the
    safety of personal information)**\n\n\"Company\" is taking the following measures
    to ensure the safety of personal information.\n\n1. duct regular self-audit In
    order to secure stability related to personal information handling, we conduct
    regular (once a quarter) audits. \n2. Encryption of personal information The
    user's password is encrypted, stored, and managed, so only you can know it, and
    important data uses separate security features such as encrypting file and transfer
    data or using file locking. \n3. Restrictions on access to personal information
    It takes necessary measures to control access to personal information by granting,
    changing, and canceling access to the database system that processes personal
    information, and controls unauthorized access from outside using the intrusion
    prevention system. \n4. Use locks for document security Documents containing
    personal information and auxiliary storage media are stored in a safe place with
    a lock.\n\n**Article 7 (Matters concerning the installation and operation of
    devices that automatically collect personal information and their rejection)**\n\n1.
    \"Company\" uses \"cookie\" to store usage information and retrieve it from time
    to time to provide individual customized services to users. \n2. Cookies are
    a small amount of information sent by the server (http) used to run the website
    to the user's computer browser and are sometimes stored on the hard disk inside
    the user's PC computer.\n3. Purpose of use of cookies: It is used to provide
    optimized information to users by identifying the type of visit and use of each
    service and website visited by users, popular search terms, security access,
    etc.\n4. Installation and Operation of Cookies: You can refuse to save cookies
    by setting options in the Tools > Internet Options > Privacy menu at the top
    of the web browser.\n5. If you refuse to save cookies, it may be difficult to
    use customized services.\n\n**Article 8** **(Personal Information Protection
    Manager)**\n\nThe company is designating a personal information protection manager
    as follows to protect the customer\u2019s personal information and process relevant
    complaints.\n\n- Position: Personal Information Protection Manager\n- Mail: devs@staika.io\n\n**Article
    9(Change of Personal Information Processing Policy)**\n\nThis privacy policy
    will take effect on January 9, 2023."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
